    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing efficiency against favorable matchups, headlined by our strongest play: **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03). Facing the lefty Abbott, **Seiya Suzuki** receives a massive +19% boost from the pitcher\u2019s skill profile, effectively weaponizing his platoon advantage to anchor our outfield. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is set to exploit a premium matchup against Baz, bolstered by a +16% park factor and +15% SP skill advantage. Our aggressive approach to stolen base potential is on full display with **Mickey Moniak** (69.68), who is an elite start today; he benefits from a +14% platoon boost and, crucially, faces a pitcher with a slow delivery, further inflating his upside in a category that remains our primary focus.\n\nWhile we remain confident in our starting nine, the decision to bench **Austin Riley** (44.70) was razor-thin. **Austin Riley** narrowly missed the cut behind **Kyle Karros** and **Isaac Paredes** primarily due to a combination of an unfavorable wind forecast and a poor historical BvP profile against May. We opted to stay within our \"Zebras Floor\" threshold, favoring the specific situational advantages of our starters over the raw baseline projection of our bench. We are tracking a few risks: **Brice Turang** faces a significant test against Skenes, and while his +6% order boost helps, his efficiency is hampered by the catcher\u2019s elite pop time. Additionally, **Edwin Arroyo** sits right on our 40.0 floor, making him a potential candidate for a late-inning sub if the game script turns negative against Boyd.",
